Data Lost ❌
Solution

Persistent Volume

What is PV?

A Persistent Volume is actual storage available to the cluster.

Think of it as:

Hard Disk for Kubernetes
Example
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolume

metadata:
  name: ecommerce-backend-pv

spec:
  capacity:
    storage: 1Gi
Commands

Get PV

kubectl get pv

Describe PV

kubectl describe pv
Persistent Volume Claim (PVC)
What is PVC?

PVC is a request for storage.

Think:

PV  = Actual Disk

PVC = Request For Disk
Example
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim

metadata:
  name: ecommerce-backend-pvc

spec:
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce

  resources:
    requests:
      storage: 1Gi
Relationship
PVC
 ↓
PV
 ↓
Storage
Your Project Example

Backend Deployment:

volumes:
  - name: ecommerce-storage
    persistentVolumeClaim:
      claimName: ecommerce-backend-pvc

Mounted:

volumeMounts:
  - name: ecommerce-storage
    mountPath: /data
Commands

Get PVC

kubectl get pvc

Describe PVC

kubectl describe pvc
