StatefulSets
What is a StatefulSet?

A StatefulSet is used for applications that need:

Stable Identity
Persistent Storage
Ordered Startup
Ordered Shutdown

Examples:

MySQL
PostgreSQL
MongoDB
Kafka
Redis Cluster
Why Not Deployment?

Deployment Pods are interchangeable.

Example:

backend-pod-x7a
backend-pod-y8b

If one dies:

New Random Pod Created

Perfect for stateless apps.

But databases need:

Fixed Hostname
Fixed Storage
StatefulSet Architecture
StatefulSet
      |
      |
      +------ mysql-0
      |
      +------ mysql-1

Unlike Deployments:

backend-xyz
backend-abc
backend-pqr
