Security Best Practices
1. Least Privilege Principle

Grant only required permissions.

Bad:

Cluster Admin Everywhere ❌

Good:

Read Only Access ✅
2. Use Service Accounts

Avoid:

Default Service Account

Create dedicated accounts.

Example:

frontend-sa
backend-sa
monitoring-sa
3. Protect Secrets

Avoid:

DB_PASSWORD: password123

Use:

Kubernetes Secrets
4. Use Network Policies

Restrict communication.

Example:

Frontend → Backend ✅

Frontend → MySQL ❌
5. Restrict Namespace Access

Example:

Developer

Should not access:

kube-system
6. Regularly Rotate Credentials

Rotate:

JWT Secret
API Keys
Database Passwords
